@startuml hld-01b_module_dependencies
title HLD-01b — Module dependencies, DETAIL (UML **component diagram** with provided and required interfaces)\nA lollipop (—O) is an interface the component **provides**; a dashed «use» arrow is one it **requires**.\nA module's `contracts` sub-package is exactly its set of provided interfaces. The package-level picture is HLD-01a.
skinparam wrapWidth 170
skinparam componentStyle uml2

component market_data <<Supporting>> #LightGreen
component strategy <<Core Domain>> #Gold
component trading <<Supporting>> #LightGreen
component backtesting <<Supporting>> #LightGreen
component charting <<Generic>> #White
component indicators <<Generic>> #White
component binance_gateway <<Generic>> #White

package "market_data.contracts" <<provided>> {
  interface IHistoricalKlines
  interface IMarketStream
  interface IMarketDataSync
  interface IRangeCoverage
}
package "trading.contracts" <<provided>> {
  interface IOrderSubmission
  interface ITradingSession
  interface IAccountSnapshot
}
package "strategy.contracts" <<provided>> {
  interface IStrategyCatalog
  interface IStrategyEngineFactory
}
package "support.contracts" <<provided>> {
  interface IChartHost
  interface IIndicatorCatalog
  interface ITradingSessionFactory
}

market_data -down- IHistoricalKlines
market_data -down- IMarketStream
market_data -down- IMarketDataSync
market_data -down- IRangeCoverage

trading -down- IOrderSubmission
trading -down- ITradingSession
trading -down- IAccountSnapshot

strategy -down- IStrategyCatalog
strategy -down- IStrategyEngineFactory

charting -up- IChartHost
indicators -up- IIndicatorCatalog
binance_gateway -up- ITradingSessionFactory

strategy ..> IHistoricalKlines : <<use>>
strategy ..> IMarketStream : <<use>>
strategy ..> IOrderSubmission : <<use>>
strategy ..> ITradingSession : <<use>>
strategy ..> IAccountSnapshot : <<use>>
strategy ..> IChartHost : <<use>>
strategy ..> IIndicatorCatalog : <<use>>

trading ..> IHistoricalKlines : <<use>>
trading ..> IMarketStream : <<use>>
trading ..> IMarketDataSync : <<use>>
trading ..> IChartHost : <<use>>
trading ..> ITradingSessionFactory : <<use>>

backtesting ..> IHistoricalKlines : <<use>>
backtesting ..> IMarketDataSync : <<use>>
backtesting ..> IRangeCoverage : <<use>>
backtesting ..> IStrategyCatalog : <<use>>
backtesting ..> IStrategyEngineFactory : <<use>>
backtesting ..> IChartHost : <<use>>
backtesting ..> IIndicatorCatalog : <<use>>

market_data ..> ITradingSessionFactory : <<use>>

note right of market_data
  **Open Host Service + Published Language.** market_data publishes one
  set of interfaces for all three downstream contexts, spoken in `core.vo`
  (MarketData, TimeFrame) plus the signal MarketTickEvent.
end note

note left of strategy
  **Customer/Supplier, twice over.** trading supplies strategy
  (IOrderSubmission, ITradingSession, IAccountSnapshot) and strategy
  supplies backtesting (IStrategyCatalog, IStrategyEngineFactory).
  In both pairs the supplier does not know its customer exists —
  **trading never requires anything strategy provides**, which is
  what keeps the two acyclic. The cycle is broken by a trading-owned
  concept: the symbol lease, ITradingSession.claim_symbol.
end note

note bottom of binance_gateway
  **Anticorruption Layer.** binance_gateway is the only component
  permitted to construct `binance.client.Client` (an existing guard
  test). market_data and trading each wrap their own half of the SDK
  in their own `adapters` — REST klines and the market websocket on
  one side, futures REST and the user-data websocket on the other.
end note

note bottom of charting
  **Conformist.** A component draws through IChartHost using charting's
  own MarkerPoint / RegionSpan / InfoField types, with no translation
  layer of its own.
end note

note bottom of backtesting
  **Anticorruption Layer inside backtesting.** strategy owns its
  StrategyContext (candles plus the current position, as a neutral value
  object); backtesting translates PaperExchange into it, and trading
  builds the same context from LivePosition. Today three strategies still
  import `domain/backtesting` — the wrong direction — and that is the
  dependency this ACL removes.
end note
@enduml
